{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/783568-crossover-conversion-question-would-beasts-register-on-sense-wyrm","id":783568,"title":"Crossover/Conversion Question: Would Beasts Register on \"Sense Wyrm\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-10T12:12:59-08:00","id":783568,"title":"Crossover/Conversion Question: Would Beasts Register on \"Sense Wyrm\"","content":"Dear Onyx<br /> Since *official* &quot;Conversion Manuals&quot; that allow you to incorporate/switch/adapt elements of Vampire/Werewolf/Changeling ACROSS the Worlds Of Darkness have been released, it stands to reason that this situation would eventually pop up on some gaming table in the future.<br /> <br /> The Garou Gift &quot;Sense Wyrm&quot; is a radar that &quot;pings&quot; (so to speak) when a Person/Creature/Spirit &quot;Stinks of the Wyrm&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, a Wyrm Spirit LITERALLY feeds on the Enrgies of Pain, Fear and Suffering.<br /> Much like a Beast Does, coincidentally<br /> <br /> Hence, should a Garou use &quot;Sense Wyrm&quot; when in the presence of Beasts, would they be marked as &quot;Of The Wyrm&quot; much like Vampires of Humanity 6 or Lower?<br /> <br /> Insomnically<br /> Lin Liren.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T16:17:04-08:00","id":783733,"title":"","content":"Looking it over I don't think it would be unreasonable to presume that they might trip it. Though how strongly one &quot;stinks&quot; would probably vary with some ,probably uncommon to rare as heck, Beasts who come off as only having the incidental smell of Wyrm due to striving to be the top of a company that just happens to be Wyrm tainted, to those who probably reek of Wyrm like a ravager who's most recent feed was ensuring a lethal plague outbreak started in a hospital.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T18:48:26-08:00","id":783827,"title":"","content":"Like anything else, depends on the kind of game you're gonna run. If Beasts are prime for being Antagonists to a werewolf game, go with it. If you wanna foster player versus player in a divided playerbase, go for it. If the Beast and werewolves are supposed to work together... I'd advice against this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T23:51:23-08:00","id":783964,"title":"","content":"My two cents: Beasts would probably &quot;smell&quot; similar to however Unseelie Fae &quot;smell&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 12-13-2015, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T06:39:41-08:00","id":785364,"title":"","content":"I'm inclined to say hell yes. Destructiveness is at the core of their life cycle, no matter how ethically they try to live with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T08:35:21-08:00","id":785407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/783568-crossover-conversion-question-would-beasts-register-on-sense-wyrm?p=785364#post785364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm inclined to say hell yes. Destructiveness is at the core of their life cycle, no matter how ethically they try to live with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm.. I'd say they smell like Humans are supposed too. Perfectly in Balance.. Even if they are about Destruction and Fear they do it for a Higher purpose so that Growth can come and old Concepts can be learned from.<br /> <br /> Obviously that's just the Generalisation and they would likely be easy too corrupt (Maybe they got mostly turned and there are only afew left... The Formora are their Children?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T07:10:41-08:00","id":785945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/783568-crossover-conversion-question-would-beasts-register-on-sense-wyrm?p=785407#post785407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm.. I'd say they smell like Humans are supposed too. Perfectly in Balance.. Even if they are about Destruction and Fear they do it for a Higher purpose so that Growth can come and old Concepts can be learned from.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what the Wyrm is supposed to be, but it does that by being the Wyrm. Or to put it another way, your argument still makes me thing they'd smell like the Wyrm, but they'd be part of the reason why <i>humans</i> are (meant to be) balanced.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T09:13:17-08:00","id":786017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/783568-crossover-conversion-question-would-beasts-register-on-sense-wyrm?p=785945#post785945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what the Wyrm is supposed to be, but it does that by being the Wyrm. Or to put it another way, your argument still makes me thing they'd smell like the Wyrm, but they'd be part of the reason why <i>humans</i> are (meant to be) balanced.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't say they Wouldn't smell of the wyrm, just they'd smell like anyone else smells of the wyrm. In the oWoD i always read it that EVERYTHING about modern Human society smells of the wyrm, that everything could be a pawn corrupted into destructive ends because the wyrm can't act how its supposed too, if the trinity was working fine then humans wouldn't have sleepers, vampires wouldn't be around and the world would be alot brighter in general. However because of the Weaver the Wyrm is trapped and in pain.. things in pain don't act rationally and hence it's thrashing at the strings/bindings are tainting everything they are connected to. (Like the entire world) Everything Smells of the Wyrm... Even the Garou themselves stink of the Wyrm.. but they are so used to the smell upon themselves that it's not something they consider anymore. It takes something REALLY Strong in stench to get them to notice it.<br /> <br /> Beast's would smell like anyone else does MAYBE alittle more then average if they are heavily active in feeding/feasting on the fears of others... Although I'd also say that a Beast in the oWoD would never go hungry... So much fear and anger and the like in the background of the world that they could get by on family dinners literally all the time...<br /> <br /> My thoughts on the matter even if I could be considered wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T15:09:49-08:00","id":786285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/783568-crossover-conversion-question-would-beasts-register-on-sense-wyrm?p=785945#post785945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what the Wyrm is supposed to be, but it does that by being the Wyrm. Or to put it another way, your argument still makes me thing they'd smell like the Wyrm, but they'd be part of the reason why <i>humans</i> are (meant to be) balanced.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You know, that gives me an interesting idea. Beasts are children of the Wyrm that are for some reason trying to continue fulfilling the Wyrm's original purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}